# Add as GitHub Actions secrets (Settings → Secrets → Actions):
# GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=your_google_api_key
#
# Recommended for numbered UK door addresses when typing a street name:
# GETADDRESS_DOMAIN_TOKEN=dtoken_...   (create at https://getaddress.io — restrict to your domain)
#
# In Google Cloud, restrict the key to HTTP referrers:
#   https://www.myairporttaxini.co.uk/*
#   https://myairporttaxini.co.uk/*
#
# Enable in Google Cloud (APIs & Services → Library):
#   - Places API (New)
# The route map uses OpenStreetMap and does not need Maps Embed API.
#
# --- Google Calendar booking log (Cloudflare Worker secrets) ---
# Website bookings (desktop email + mobile WhatsApp) are written to your Google Calendar
# by the Cloudflare Worker. Add these with `wrangler secret put`:
#
#   GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID
#     Your calendar ID — usually your Gmail address (e.g. you@gmail.com).
#     Find it in Google Calendar → Settings → [calendar] → Integrate calendar.
#
#   GOOGLE_CALENDAR_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON
#     Full JSON key for a Google Cloud service account with Calendar API enabled.
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. In Google Cloud Console, enable "Google Calendar API".
#   2. Create a service account and download its JSON key.
#   3. Open Google Calendar → Settings → share your calendar with the service
#      account email (…@….iam.gserviceaccount.com) as "Make changes to events".
#   4. Store the secrets on the Worker:
#        cd workers/addresses
#        npx wrangler secret put GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID
#        npx wrangler secret put GOOGLE_CALENDAR_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON
#
# BOOKINGS_API_URL (GitHub Actions secret) must point at the Worker /bookings URL
# for calendar logging to run in production.
